<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan central bank takes 1.99 bln rupees in OMO.</title>
<headline>Pakistan central bank takes 1.99 bln rupees in OMO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank said on Wednesday it had accepted 1.99 billion rupees in Short Term Federal Bonds in an open market operation. Figures in brackets show results of the last OMO on November 27.</p>
<p>		     Offered	 Accepted	Max cut-off</p>
<p>Outright sales   2,140 (6,085) 1,990 (5,320) 16.45 pct/yr (15.0)</p>
<p>Five-month REPO   none		none	  none</p>
<p>Three-month REPO  none		none	  none</p>
<p>One-month REPO    none		none	  none</p>
<p>Total(million rupees)2,140	   1,300</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
